# Fields:
#   id          unique short id ("rk"=answerable knowledge, "rx"=must-refuse: off-corpus or advice/opinion)
#   query       the raw user question
#   source      exact index title the answer should come from; null when the guard must refuse
#               valid titles (must match build_rag_index.py exactly):
#                 Real Estate Data Analyst Primer | Trestle Property Metadata |
#                 Market Summaries Data | MLS Schema Reference
#   answerable  true -> expect a grounded answer; false -> expect the exact refusal string
#   note        optional free-text reminder to yourself
#
# Labels reflect where the answer SHOULD live, not what retrieve() happens to return —
# a gold source missing from the top-k is a retrieval failure to report, not a label to change.
